API-14: range-check a link status before converting it to char

EN_setlinkvalue(EN_INITSTATUS or EN_STATUS) rounded the value and cast
it to char before checking that it is 0 or 1. Values such as 256 and
257 wrapped to 0 and 1 and were accepted, so 256 closed the link with
return code 0. Check the value itself, before the conversion.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-14_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..ae62863 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -4206,8 +4206,9 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinkvalue(EN_Project p, int index, int property, double valu
         // Status 's' must be either EN_CLOSED (0) or EN_OPEN (1)
         // (to set the status of a valve to ACTIVE, assign a value to its
         // EN_INITSETTING or EN_SETTING property)
+        // (written so that NaN is refused too)
+        if (!(value >= 0.0 && value <= 1.0)) return 211;
         s = (char)ROUND(value);
-        if (s < 0 || s > 1) return 211;
 
         if (property == EN_INITSTATUS)
         {
